This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: If some living foo creature is hit with turn-undead, it should
turn undead (ie. turn into a zombie foo). --azgor

[2]: Rings of regeneration can have an enchantment - the higher the
enchantment the more it regenerates per turn and the more nutrition it
uses. Negatively enchanted rings sap your life to fill your belly
(doubly dangerous - death by choking or by life drain.) --Grunt

[3]: Wand of inversion a la Beyond Zork: turn containers and creatures
temporarily inside out, expelling their contents --aioli

[4]: If you drop the amulet of yendor on astral and one of the NPCs
gets it, then they should try and sacrifice it to their god --scwizard

[5]: Death messages involving wands should include who/what zapped the
wand. --SheeEttin

[6]: Tinning the corpse of a named creature should make the tin be
named. --SomeoneElseYes

[7]: Cursed grease should never wear off and should only come off your
hands with a blessed towel. --azgor

[8]: Tigers should have a slim chance of dropping tiger eye rings.
--greqrg

[9]: Add a donut food item for Keystone Kops to be sometimes generated
with --rmckay

[10]: Pack animals. If you have a pet quadruped and a spare bag, you
should be able to attach the bag to the animal and let it haul things
for you. --azgor

[11]: Shrinking and growing akin to Alice in Wonderland. If you were
large, or a monster was shrunken, you could squish the enemy under
foot. I believe Alice's clothes grew and shrank with her. I don't know
if this should be changed for nethack. Changing it would result in
thinkgs like, "The gnome lord suddenly shrinks right out of its
clothes. You step on the tiny naked gnome lord." --azgor

[12]: wishing for sex should summon foocubi --Botje

[13]: and "boy{s,friend}" or "girl{s,friend}" foocubi of the
appropriate gender --cjeris

[14]: Bribing certain greedy monsters can tame them altogether; could
work especially well if you're the same race. --Grunt

[15]: killing kittens should increase alignment if chaotic --Botje

[16]: Monster: swarm of biting flies - this would occupy multiple
contiguous squares. Weapons other than fire brand would have no effect.
Your best hope is to get the swarm into a corridor and zap the lot with
fire. If you bisect a swarm with fire, the unaffected squares become
two swarms, but if they touch, they merge into one swarm. Doesn't do
much damage, but is impossible to kill without a source of fire or gas.
Low level players will probably need to try to get a closed door
between them and the swarm to have any hope.  Causes blindness if you
are surrounded by the swarm.  --azgor


